    <briefdescription>
<para>Gradient function for raising a tensor to an integer power. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradExponent" kindref="compound">GradExponent</ref> class represents the exponentiation operation in the computational graph, computing gradients for raising a tensor to an integer power. For the operation <formula id="35">$C = A^n$</formula> where <formula id="12">$A$</formula> is a tensor and <formula id="36">$n$</formula> is an integer exponent, the gradient computation follows from the power rule:   <formula id="37">\[    \frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = n \cdot A^{n-1}
\]</formula></para>
<para>During backpropagation, the incoming gradient  <formula id="8">$\frac{\partial L}{\partial
C}$</formula> is multiplied elementwise with the derivative according to the chain rule:     <formula id="38">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \odot
\frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = \frac{\partial L}{\partial C} \odot (n
\cdot A^{n-1})
\]</formula></para>
<para>This <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> saves the input tensor and the integer exponent from the forward pass as both are required to compute the gradient during the backward pass using the power rule.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> for the base class from which this class derives. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradExponential" kindref="compound">GradExponential</ref> for the gradient function for the natural exponential function. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
